    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d748">

                <pb facs="0821" n="701" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg701"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.48/3831: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ortiz Rubio</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to President Hoover</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-21T20:45:00-07:00">January 21, 1931—8:45
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 22—12:29 a.m.]<anchor n="1"
                            xml:id="d748-f1"/></dateline></opener>
                <p>On behalf of the people of my country I deeply thank you for the sympathy which
                    you were pleased to extend to the Mexican Nation in <pb facs="0822" n="702"
                        xml:id="pg702"/> the name of the noble American Nation. On my own part I
                    also thank the people of the United States for their expression of sympathy as
                    well as you for the personal sentiments you express as their worthy Chief
                    Magistrate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. Ortiz Rubio</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d748-f1" n="1" xml:id="d748-f1-content">
                <p>Received in the Department of State on January 26.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
